From feb1b71e4669890b22dabc08ba6375ef5a738eae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:31:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: native 3D by default again, batched (one depth and one
 colour pass per run of opaque faces); 960x544 widescreen; render size,
 smoothing, 30 fps and PGXP switches

- Renderer3D::DrawUpto with THPS_R3D_BATCH (default on, ES only): every face up to the next 2D
  primitive goes to GlGpu::LayerBatch as one vertex range. The opaque faces' true depth first
  (colour masked), then their colour against it with the 1/256 decal tolerance (painter order
  inside it, so decals over coplanar floors still win), then semi-transparent and subtractive
  faces in their order. The draw vertex shader's u_dpass carries a class select (+2 x sel) that
  moves the other classes' triangles outside the clip volume. Faces with an HD texture keep the
  old draws. [gl] counts "batched".
- The Vita's default 3D is the native renderer again (t17's PS1 path at 728x544: 27 fps and
  affine warping); THPS_RENDER3D=psx is the PS1 path. Gameplay is 16:9 at 960x544 (WidePad)
  unless THPS_WIDESCREEN=0.
- pc_vitagfx.h: PC_VitaGfxGet(), the Vita graphics settings from env.txt (THPS_VITA_RES=WxH of
  512x240/720x408/960x544, THPS_WIDESCREEN, THPS_FILTER, THPS_VITA_FPS=30|60, THPS_RENDER3D). The
  GRAPHICS menu that will edit them in Settings.ini is a later patch.
- GlGpu: surfaces sized within the render size (scaled up when shown); SMOOTHING applies to
  gameplay screens only (menus stay smooth); [gl] start-up line with screen, render size,
  widescreen, smoothing, fps.
- FrameClock: locked 30 shows every other frame (the game still runs at 60).
- THPS_PGXP=0: THPS_GL_PRECISE=0 + THPS_GL_PERSPECTIVE=0; [gl] PGXP line at start.
- No render thread: every GL call is made inside the game's VSync callback while the OT is
  walked, and readbacks feed the game synchronously; recording all of it is left for later.
